<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charter Oath</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Charter Oath was a statement of five principles promulgated in 1868 at the start of the Meiji era in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the name of the young emperor. It promised deliberative assemblies, the participation of all classes, the abandonment of outdated customs and the seeking of knowledge throughout the world. It set out the programme of reform from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> emerged.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charter-oath.jpg" alt="Charter Oath" width="235" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Japan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5jo1.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
